    "q-337219": {
      "dom_id": "step-q337219",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}5t \\\\ 7t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">$x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+\\,\\,\\frac{1}{4}$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$8t-14$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">.</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nNotice that we are given that\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}.\n$$\n\nWe'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & 2{e}^{2t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-t} & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5t \\\\ 7t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{-t}\\cdot {e}^{2t}-2{e}^{2t}\\cdot 2{e}^{-t}}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & -2{e}^{2t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-t} & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{3}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & -2{e}^{2t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-t} & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-2t} & -{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-2t} & -{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5t \\\\ 7t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3t{e}^{t} \\\\ t{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}3t{e}^{t} \\\\ t{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int 3t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int t{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating the components by parts, we get the following:\n\n- For the first component, let $u=3t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=3\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v={e}^{t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(3t)\\cdot {e}^{t}-\\int {e}^{t}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =3t{e}^{t}-3{e}^{t} \\\\  & =3{e}^{t}(t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, let $u=t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=1\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int t{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(t)\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{2})\\cdot (1\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{t{e}^{-2t}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{4}(2t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & 2{e}^{2t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-t} & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{t}(t-1) \\\\ -\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{4}(2t+1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}12(t-1)-2(2t+1) \\\\ 24(t-1)-(2t+1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}8t-14 \\\\ 22t-25\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
